# Test: a live edit of service dns-resolver allow-from reaches the running
#       resolver on the next query.
# Initial config: allow-from 127.0.0.1/32.
# After SIGHUP:   allow-from 127.0.0.2/32, nothing else changed.
# Expected: the reload completes, a query from 127.0.0.1 is refused and a
#           query from 127.0.0.2 is answered, on the listener the boot config
#           bound.
#
# Spec: spec-lan-dns-resolver (closed 2026-10-28) -- AC-30
# VALIDATES: the resolver's verify/apply pair (internal/plugins/dnsresolver/
#            config_tx.go) publishes the reloaded policy to the query path: a
#            source the reload removed is refused (RFC-less policy, AC-2's
#            check) and a source it added is answered through the forwarder.
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload, where the commit succeeds and the
#           resolver keeps serving the boot allow-from until a restart: a LAN
#           prefix the operator withdrew keeps its access.
#
# That the listeners are not rebound by a policy-only reload is proven in Go
# by TestReloadKeepsListeners (internal/plugins/dnsresolver/config_tx_test.go):
# a datagram exchanged on one socket across the reload. Here the same address
# and port answer before and after it.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: client/dns-query asks from 127.0.0.1 until the reply is
# REFUSED, and only the reloaded allow-from refuses that source. A resolver
# that kept the boot policy answers NOERROR until the fixture gives up, and
# seq=5 from 127.0.0.2 is REFUSED: both red. A resolver that refused everyone
# fails seq=5.
#
# The trigger copies config2.conf over ze-bgp.conf and sends SIGHUP once the
# daemon is ready; the query steps do not wait for it, so the first asks until
# the reloaded answer arrives.
#
# No cmd= line carries `:timeout=`: a foreground command's timeout replaces
# option=timeout as the budget of the whole test (resolveOrchestratedTimeout,
# internal/test/runner/runner_exec_util.go), so the daemon's or the last
# query's would become the reload's whole budget.

option=timeout:value=40s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
	dns-resolver {
		enabled true
		listener lan {
			ip 127.0.0.1
			port $PORT
		}
		allow-from 127.0.0.1/32
		forward {
			server 127.0.0.1 {
				port $PORT2
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
service {
	dns-resolver {
		enabled true
		listener lan {
			ip 127.0.0.1
			port $PORT
		}
		allow-from 127.0.0.2/32
		forward {
			server 127.0.0.1 {
				port $PORT2
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le mock dns --port $PORT2
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=le test fixture client/dns-query 127.0.0.1:$PORT web.example.test. A REFUSED
expect=stderr:contains=OK: dns A web.example.test. served REFUSED
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=le dns query --server 127.0.0.1:$PORT --source 127.0.0.2 --name web.example.test --type A --rd
expect=stdout:contains=rcode NOERROR
expect=stdout:contains=203.0.113.10
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
